        <body>
            
            <div type="edition" xml:lang="tam-Latn" rendition="class:tamil maturity:83215">
                
                <ab>
                    <lb n="1"/><hi rend="grantha">svasti śrī </hi> <g ref="sym:tam-pillaiyarCuli" type="symbol">*</g>
                </ab>
                <p>
                    tiru viṉai turai
                    <lb n="2"/>periyamāṉ āḻ<supplied reason="omitted">vā</supplied>r
                </p>
                
            </div>
            
            <div type="apparatus">
                <listApp>
                    
                    <app loc="1">
                        <lem>periyamāṉ āḻ<supplied reason="omitted">vā</supplied>r</lem>
                        <rdg source="bib:Ramachandran1954_01">periyamāṉ ā<choice><sic>ma</sic><corr>ḷvā</corr></choice>r</rdg>
                    </app>
                    
                </listApp>
            </div>
            
            <div type="translation" source="bib:Ramachandran1954_01">
                
                <p n="1">Hail! Prosperity!</p>
                <p n="1-2">The devotee <supplied reason="explanation"><foreign>Āḻvār</foreign></supplied> of the Lord <supplied reason="explanation">Buddha</supplied> who annihilates <foreign>karma</foreign>.</p>			
                
            </div>
            
            <div type="translation" resp="part:emfr">
             
            </div>
            
            <div type="commentary">
                <p><bibl><ptr target="bib:Ramachandran1954_01"/></bibl> comments thus: <quote>The donor (<foreign>Āḻvār</foreign>) is announced as dedicating the image so that Lord Buddha can help him annihilate his <foreign>karma</foreign>. <foreign>periyamāṉ</foreign> = <foreign>perumāṉ</foreign> may also be the name of the donor.</quote></p>
            </div>
            
            <div type="bibliography">
                
                <p>Edited in <bibl><ptr target="bib:Ramachandran1954_01"/></bibl>, with a facsimile (p. 86, no. 60 and pl. XXV, no. 23). See also <bibl><ptr target="bib:Ramachandran1965_01"/></bibl>, <bibl><ptr target="bib:Ramachandran1992_01"/></bibl>, <bibl><ptr target="bib:Ramachandran2005_01"/></bibl> (p. 102, no. 60 and pl. IV, no. 23).</p>
                <p>Edited and translated here by Emmanuel Francis, based on <bibl><ptr target="bib:Ramachandran1954_01"/></bibl> and the facsimile therein.</p>
                
